[112.171147, "o", "  A1  stopped  weights replaced in storage after signing (the community quant's weights)\r\n  A2  stopped  a file added after signing: custom code next to the weights (holds only the lab marker)\r\n  A3  stopped  the signature deleted, so there is nothing to check\r\n  A4  stopped  weights swapped, then re-signed with the attacker's own key, and that key shipped as keys/ci.pub\r\n  A5  stopped  an old release (1.0.0), validly signed by our own CI key, revoked since: replayed into the deploy step\r\n  A6  stopped  a 'smaller, just as good' community quant handed to CI to ship instead of our own int8\r\n  A7  stopped  the signature file damaged, so the check throws an error instead of saying no\r\n  N1  deploys  a clean release of our own int8 build\r\n  N2  deploys  a clean release whose README was written BEFORE signing\r\n  N3  deploys  the same clean release deployed twice (a retried pipeline): both succeed, one registry version\r\n\r\nAttacks that worked: 0 of 7  (none) | normal releases that deploy: 3 of 3\r\n"]
